# Keep line endings predictable across machines.
#
# A shell script checked out with Windows endings fails to run at all -- the
# interpreter line ends up as "#!/usr/bin/env sh\r" -- so the launcher must stay
# LF. The Windows batch file is the opposite case and wants CRLF.
* text=auto eol=lf
*.sh text eol=lf
*.cmd text eol=crlf
